    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1385",
      "reading_order": 1786,
      "section": "Catalytic Converters",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 215.28,
        "t": 564.9060195312501,
        "r": 560.7,
        "b": 532.3383344167462
      },
      "content": "Once the fan motor assembly has been removed from the rear of the cavity, the four  M7  hex  nuts  should  be  removed  at the  rear  of  the  cavity  (inside)  to  allow removal of the internal box and catalytic converters.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_1782",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_6",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_6",
          "title": "6 Replacing components"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_1782",
          "title": "Catalytic Converters"
        }
      ],
      "page": 100,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1386",
      "reading_order": 1787,
      "section": "Catalytic Converters",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 36.0,
        "t": 488.10601953125,
        "r": 276.54299999999995,
        "b": 467.3013344167462
      },
      "content": "The upper catalyst is fitted using two M7 hex flange nuts, tightened to 2.1 Nm.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_1782",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_6",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_6",
          "title": "6 Replacing components"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_1782",
          "title": "Catalytic Converters"
        }
      ],
      "page": 100,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
